     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hey all,<div><br></div><div>I posted this question on twitter - see this link for the thread that includes a few other options.  Consensus seems to be what Matthew specified above, though.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://twitter.com/Voovarb/status/1102620096428535808\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://twitter.com/Voovarb/status/1102620096428535808&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466087565000&amp;usg=AOvVaw17eTdSGydyECi3L4IwOC5r\">https://twitter.com/Voovarb/status/1102620096428535808</a><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Mar 4, 2019 at 11:18 AM Matthieu Stigler &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mmst...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi</div><div><br></div><div>It does not seem that there is indeed a simple and clean solution. Building on John, one solution is to redefine scale_colour_discrete based on your choice. Note you need to redefine it for each scale you are likely to use (fill, colour, in discrete and continuous versions)</div><div><br></div><div><div><pre style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:none 0% 0% repeat scroll rgb(248,248,248);display:block\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">library</span>(ggplot2)\r\nqplot(data=iris, Petal.Length, Petal.Width, color=Species, size=I(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">4</span>))\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em\"><img src=\"https://ci4.googleusercontent.com/proxy/FXlvU2W_iFxLMgtSWtEq-iCd7mXF_A10Uk63nJNT2OF2cQkv57eTSMF_0wSJzHcd-ZE=s0-d-e1-ft#https://i.imgur.com/VjSI1uk.png\" alt=\"\"></p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:none 0% 0% repeat scroll rgb(248,248,248);display:block\">\r\ncolors_i_want &lt;- c(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;yellow&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;pink&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;green&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;orange&quot;</span>)\r\nscale_colour_discrete &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">...</span>) scale_colour_manual(<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">...</span>, values = colors_i_want)\r\nscale_fill_discrete &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">...</span>) scale_fill_manual(<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">...</span>, values = colors_i_want)\r\n\r\nlast_plot()\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em\"><img src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/bF4_HefD6QkObf_y1_pK7vrBeJpzmfFwU6NcXIaL-v_DvnU3NT6FQMqOh2A3azTtkkA=s0-d-e1-ft#https://i.imgur.com/9qAsfl2.png\" alt=\"\"></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:YGBgIHI8YnI+bGlicmFyeShnZ3Bsb3QyKTxicj5xcGxvdChkYXRhPWlyaXMsIFBldGFsLkxlbmd0\r\naCwgUGV0YWwuV2lkdGgsIGNvbG9yPVNwZWNpZXMsIHNpemU9SSg0KSk8YnI+YGBgPGJyPjxicj4h\r\nW10oaHR0cHM6Ly9pLmltZ3VyLmNvbS9WalNJMXVrLnBuZyk8YnI+PGJyPmBgYCByPGJyPjxicj48\r\nYnI+Y29sb3JzX2lfd2FudCAmbHQ7LSBjKCJ5ZWxsb3ciLCAicGluayIsICJncmVlbiIsICJvcmFu\r\nZ2UiKTxicj5zY2FsZV9jb2xvdXJfZGlzY3JldGUgJmx0Oy0gZnVuY3Rpb24oLi4uKSBzY2FsZV9j\r\nb2xvdXJfbWFudWFsKC4uLiwgdmFsdWVzID0gY29sb3JzX2lfd2FudCk8YnI+c2NhbGVfZmlsbF9k\r\naXNjcmV0ZSAmbHQ7LSBmdW5jdGlvbiguLi4pIHNjYWxlX2ZpbGxfbWFudWFsKC4uLiwgdmFsdWVz\r\nID0gY29sb3JzX2lfd2FudCk8YnI+PGJyPmxhc3RfcGxvdCgpPGJyPmBgYDxicj48YnI+IVtdKGh0\r\ndHBzOi8vaS5pbWd1ci5jb20vOXFBc2ZsMi5wbmcp\" style=\"min-height:0px;width:0px;max-height:0px;max-width:0px;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0px;margin:0px\"></div></div><br></div></div></div></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Mar 4, 2019 at 10:52 AM John Mola &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">john...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I guess it depends on how complex of a solution you need? I recently started just definining colors at the beginning of my markdown scripts by just creating a vector of the colors I want. So just something like:<div><br></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">colors_i_want &lt;- c(&quot;red&quot;, &quot;blue&quot;, &quot;green&quot;, &quot;orange&quot;) </font></div><div><br></div><div>then later on I just add</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">scale_fill_manual(values = colors_i_want)</font></div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Someone will likely give you a more sophisticated answer but </font><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">if that&#39;s all you need I see no reason to make it more complicated. If you know you&#39;re using scale_fill_manual over and over, you could even save that into the object :)</span></div><div></div><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/qfjyL3TDosfXClg428SIPQWPjhYCru_2Tr0L6AG2iiD2OjOeGhbscbtPRaJSATK_5dsEhFg8PV1gV0tSYMDk2Cw1BpZ_uAHBtJZzi2RUy11ctn_W0aJq4R3UjJuZJ6KiWDNGxAMZqfWxYIW6N5UiovPEhApbvlsW9r3W-NEqf1AX9B-KHcbH4in3VNdKzaunnYWFKHa8yw5pqmXLMZdHohVgbGCiPdna6UR4hYaR=s0-d-e1-ft#https://gml.email/v3.2/t/image/MTU1MTcyNTM2MjUyNjY0MzcyNTIxN2ExNmZkNjRhNTQzNzJhOTRhNWZhJmpvaG5tbW9sYUBnbWFpbC5jb20mZGF2aXMtcnVnQGdvb2dsZWdyb3Vwcy5jb20.gif\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></span></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Mar 4, 2019 at 9:12 AM &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jmle...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello!<div><br></div><div>I understand how to customize colors in a variety of ways in ggplot, but is there a way to set a palette for a session? </div><div><br></div><div>I am looking for something easy that could be added to the beginning of a script instead of building a color vector, using scale_fill_manual(), etc.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you!</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nCheck out our R resources at <a href=\"http://d-rug.github.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://d-rug.github.io/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466087565000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2a2MOD2AISnG28isV51bM4\">http://d-rug.github.io/</a><br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Davis R Users&#39; Group&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">davis-rug+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466087565000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1kWJvC9KgQmb5S_VhN8wSg\">https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466087565000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3gQJbnYOmBcETJFBW05zAz\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">John M. Mola<br></div><div><a href=\"http://johnmola.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirectur